Mon Oct  5 06:49:31 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Update to 0.0.22
  * New receiver chains for BeiDou B1C and B2a RNSS, QZSS L1 C/B and
    SBAS L1 (EGNOS, WAAS); SBAS is decoded but not yet a ranging source
  * Opt-in real-time kinematic positioning fed by RTCM 3 corrections from
    an NTRIP caster, with a new integer ambiguity resolution layer. It
    takes GPS L1 C/A alone or with L2C or L5, Galileo E1 alone or with
    E5a, and single-frequency BeiDou B1C; the client prefers NTRIP v2,
    falls back to v1, can use TLS 1.2 or newer and reports the rover
    position upstream as NMEA GGA
  * Observation and navigation files can be written in RINEX 4.02 with
    PVT.rinex_version=4; the default stays RINEX 3.02
  * New CUDA acquisition engine offloads the PCPS search grid with
    batched cuFFT. It needs a non-default build (-DENABLE_CUDA=ON) and
    is selected at run time by Acquisition_XX.use_cuda, so it is not in
    this build
  * Three new signal sources, each behind its own build flag and none
    enabled here: bladeRF without gr-osmosdr, Pocket SDR and the
    SAPHYRION EVK1029
  * Fix several group-delay and ionospheric biases in the SPP solver
  * The VOLK library subpackage is renamed libvolk_gnsssdr0_0_21 ->
    libvolk_gnsssdr0_0_22, following its SONAME libvolk_gnsssdr.so.0.0.22
  * https://github.com/gnss-sdr/gnss-sdr/releases/tag/v0.0.22
  * Many more fixes and improvements; see upstream's release notes for
    the full list

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Sun Aug 30 17:52:49 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Fix build: name the VOLK library subpackage after its SONAME,
  libvolk_gnsssdr0_0_17 -> libvolk_gnsssdr0_0_21
- Correct the license tags, per flavour, and record the components
  that are shipped but never built in a Legal-Review-Notice - upstream
  is GPL-3.0-or-later and not -only, and the binaries carry further
  licenses:
  * gnss-sdr: LGPL-3.0-only (libswiftcnav), BSD-1-Clause (supl),
    BSD-2-Clause (rtklib), BSD-3-Clause (inih), MIT (gsl-lite)
  * volk flavour: BSD-3-Clause (installed cmake files), Zlib (the
    sincos kernels)
- Build require abseil, the logging and flags backend 0.0.21 actually
  links; glog and gflags were required but unused, and abseil is only
  optional to cmake, so losing it would have switched the backend
  silently instead of failing
- Drop gnuradio from the volk flavour build requires - volk_gnsssdr is
  standalone, and the dependency left the flavour unresolvable
  wherever gnuradio is not built
- Stop building the unit tests in the default flavour, they were
  compiled and then discarded; drops the gtest build requirement
- Strip the shebang from the volk_gnsssdr_modtool modules, they are
  imported and not executed, and drop their stale sidecar bytecode
- Run the VOLK QA suite in %check, minus qa_volk_gnsssdr_32fc_convert_8ic,
  which compares the NEON kernel against generic at tolerance 0 and
  trips on a 1 LSB rounding difference on some aarch64 workers
- Declare the minimum versions upstream cmake enforces: gnuradio,
  which is fatal when older, and armadillo, matio and protobuf, where
  an older version makes cmake download sources instead
- Ship COPYING in the library and devel subpackages as well
- Let the devel subpackage require the matching library version
- Spec cleanup: drop Group tags, use %autosetup and
  %ldconfig_scriptlets, switch build dependencies to pkgconfig()

